{% from "design-system/components/section-title.njk" import sectionTitle %}
{#
  Sourcing markets: a centered row of flag chips — where a buyer's machines come from.

  Rendered as inline-block <span>s inside one mj-text rather than a column grid, so the row
  reflows on its own (6 chips do not fit on one 536px line — they wrap to 4 + 2, and to fewer
  per line on mobile) without any width maths or extra media queries.
  Outlook's Word engine ignores inline-block padding and border-radius: chips degrade there to
  bordered, square text runs — still legible, just less rounded.

  Flag badges are circular via CSS, straight off flagcdn (no asset to host). Two things matter:

  1. The size MUST be an INLINE style, not the width/height attributes. MJML's boilerplate CSS
     carries `img { height: auto }`, which outranks the attributes — leave it to them and the
     height follows each source's own aspect ratio, so the square globe icon renders taller than
     the 3:2 flags and visibly inflates its chip. Inline styles outrank embedded CSS, so
     `height:20px` here is what actually pins every badge to the same box.
     The attributes stay for blocked-image clients, which read them before any CSS applies.
  2. `object-fit:cover` fills the square without distortion; `object-position` (content.focus)
     shifts the crop for flags whose emblem is off-centre.

  Outlook's Word engine ignores border-radius, object-fit AND inline-block padding: there the chips
  are bordered text runs and the flags are squares, slightly squashed since cover cannot apply.
  Legible, just not round. Baking round PNGs would fix Outlook too, at the cost of 5 hosted assets.
#}
{$ sectionTitle('SOURCING MARKETS', tokens) $}
<mj-section padding="14px 20px 4px 20px">
  <mj-column>
    <mj-text align="center" line-height="34px" padding="0">
      {% for market in content.markets %}
      <span style="display:inline-block;margin:0 3px 8px 3px;padding:6px 13px 6px 9px;border:1px solid {$ tokens.color.hairline $};border-radius:999px;background-color:{$ tokens.color.white $};font-size:13px;font-weight:600;line-height:1;color:{$ tokens.color.heading $};white-space:nowrap;">
        <img src="{$ market.flag $}" alt="" width="20" height="20" style="display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;width:20px;height:20px;border:1px solid {$ tokens.color.hairline $};border-radius:50%;object-fit:cover;object-position:{$ market.focus | default('center') $} center;margin-right:7px;" />{$ market.label | e $}
      </span>
      {% endfor %}
    </mj-text>
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
